<title>USA: Chiron sees minimum 1996 EPS $0.25.</title>
<headline>Chiron sees minimum 1996 EPS $0.25.</headline>
<dateline>SAN FRANCISCO 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chiron Corp expects to earn a minimum of $0.25 a share for the 1996 year, said chief executive officer Edward Penhoet.</p>
<p>The First Call consensus for Chiron is $0.31 a share, with estimates ranging from $0.20 to $0.42. When asked to reconcile the $0.25 minimum goal and $0.30 Wall Street estimate, Penhoet repeated that $0.25 is the minimum it would achieve.</p>
<p>In 1995, Chiron lost $12.62 a share including a one-time $365 million write-off for inprocess technology.</p>
<p>The biopharmaceutical company earns most of its money from its diognostics group but has significant market share in vaccines and therapeutics.</p>
</text>
